 1972 and protects roughly 135 miles of free-flowing river in the Ozark Mountains. Its corridor is known for towering bluffs, paddling, hiking, fishing, swimming, wildlife and camping.</p><p>Conditions vary by season and river level. Choose an outfitter and access point that match your experience, check current conditions and rules, and leave time to explore the towns and backroads around the river.</p></article><aside class="card"><div class="stat"><b>135 mi</b><span>free-flowing river corridor</span></div><div class="stat"><b>1972</b><span>designated as America's first national river</span></div><div class="stat"><b>Ponca →</b><span>gateway to iconic upper-river scenery</span></div></aside></section><div class="head"><h2>Choose your Buffalo River experience</h2></div><section class="tiles"><a class="tile" href="/guides/buffalo-river-float-trips"><span class="num">01 · FLOAT</span><h3>Float the Buffalo</h3><p>Compare river sections, outfitters and trip styles before choosing a launch and take-out.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/things-to-do-near-buffalo-river"><span class="num">02 · ADVENTURE</span><h3>Explore the corridor</h3><p>Pair river time with overlooks, waterfalls, wildlife and nearby Ozark communities.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/best-cabins-buffalo-river"><span class="num">03 · STAY</span><h3>Book a cabin</h3><p>Stay near the river and turn a float or hiking day into a full Ozark weekend.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/best-places-to-stay-ozarks"><span class="num">04 · CAMP</span><h3>Camp under the stars</h3><p>Choose a campground or lodging base that fits your route and verify seasonal availability.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/best-hiking-ozarks"><span class="num">05 · HIKE</span><h3>Hike the bluffs</h3><p>Explore trails and overlooks while planning around weather, daylight and trail conditions.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-weekend-getaway"><span class="num">06 · WEEKEND</span><h3>Build the circuit</h3><p>Connect Buffalo River adventures with Jasper, Mountain View or other Ozark destinations.</p></a></section><div class="head"><h2>Build the trip</h2></div><section class="plans"><article class="plan"><h3>Classic float weekend</h3><p>Arrive Friday, check the river forecast and outfitter options, float Saturday and leave Sunday for a scenic hike.</p><a href="/guides/buffalo-river-float-trips">Start planning →</a></article><article class="plan"><h3>Cabin + adventure</h3><p>Use a river-area cabin as basecamp for paddling, hiking, swimming, fishing and exploring nearby towns.</p><a href="/guides/best-cabins-buffalo-river">Find cabin ideas →</a></article><article class="plan"><h3>Ozark road trip</h3><p>Make the Buffalo one stop on a longer Arkansas Ozarks loop through Jasper, Mountain View and beyond.</p><a href="/guides/best-ozarks-road-trip">Build the route →</a></article></section><section class="card owner"><h2>Own a Buffalo River business?</h2><p>Cabins, outfitters, guides, restaurants, campgrounds and attractions can claim a founding destination listing.</p><a class="btn primary" href="/list-your-cabin">Claim a free founding spot →</a></section><div class="disclosure">OzarkRoost is an independent travel directory. River levels, weather, trail conditions, access, hours and seasonal schedules can change. Verify current details with official sources and local operators before traveling. Affiliate links may earn OzarkRoost a commission at no extra cost to you.</div></main></body></html>